{
  "date": "2026-10-26",
  "scope": "Actual queue initialization, complete event/target preparation, business dispatch and final receipts; arbitrary finite event/transaction folds and exact partial failures; actual journal transaction binding and successful byte-prefix/business-history composition.",
  "properties": {
    "queue_history::initial": "All eight root tables and two arrays empty, retired_prefix zero, no other root names. Native initialization calls this same constructor.",
    "queue_history::{lookup,prepare,apply}": "The complete prepared target list is checked before business application; supplied kind is bound to event.type. Body, cache refresh and receipt finalization execute in production order. Preparation errors preserve business state; body or receipt failures retain their precisely specified partial effects.",
    "queue_history::{transaction,trace,folded}": "Every event appears in original order, with duplicates preserved. Success is the complete fold; failure identifies the exact succeeded prefix and partial failing event by index. Non-array transactions fail unchanged.",
    "queue_history::{recover,frame_trace,recovery_result}": "Skip the first identity frame when present; process every later transaction in order. Bookkeeping failure leaves business state at the prior-frame prefix; application failure includes its event index and partial transaction. No later frame executes.",
    "queue_history::{fold_join,frames_fold}": "The finite sequence of transaction folds is the same ordered flattened event fold, including empty histories and transaction boundaries.",
    "journal_state::State::apply_business": "Pass the actual borrowed State.transactions into the verified recovery loop. Native Coordinator::open calls this method; commit calls the same transaction function.",
    "journal_equivalence::physical_prefix_business": "Compose the actual State::recover and State::apply_business postconditions: successful recovered business state is the fold of the actual Values decoded from the accepted physical byte prefix, excluding its identity header. The theorem keeps the raw payload/decoded-vector relation and byte-prefix end boundary."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "The business state is the complete JSON state plus epoch, order counter and sealed flag. Derived pending/leased/usage/deadline caches and recovered-consumption bookkeeping are separate.",
    "Caches and Recovery callbacks have immutable business inputs and separately borrowed mutable objects. Their contents, termination and unwinding are unconstrained by this normal-return business proof. No whole-cache correctness or entire straw algorithm is trusted.",
    "Native Journal::open header/run validation, File/lock/fencing/context binding, callback implementation semantics, outer quarantine and cache consistency remain separate implementation obligations.",
    "The WAL theorem uses actual successful parser Values. It does not replace them by independent parses based on finite observations, which do not model all numeric representation details. Existing serde/String/Device/SHA boundaries remain explicit; no new trusted primitive.",
    "API request authorization/freshness, root extraction, closure/catalog ownership, native distributed composition and crashed-writer retirement remain unfinished.",
    "No new valid-API defect is claimed. Recovery removes its prior complete-history clone; no new I/O or persisted-format change is introduced. Performance remains deferred."
  ],
